# What EAS Build uploads.
#
# `.gitignore` is not enough here. `mobile/` is a subdirectory of the KFD
# repository, and the build archive still swept up `ios/` (1.2 GB) and
# `node_modules/` (657 MB) even though both are ignored -- only 5.4 MB of this
# directory is tracked. The result was a 74.5 MB tarball whose upload kept
# dying near the end (`write EPIPE` at 72.9 MB and 70.0 MB) on a normal home
# connection, which reads as a build failure but never reached the builder.
#
# EAS prebuilds the native projects and installs dependencies itself, so none
# of the generated output belongs in the archive. Keep this list in step with
# `.gitignore`; this file replaces it for archiving, it does not add to it.

# dependencies (installed on the builder from package-lock.json)
node_modules/

# generated native projects (EAS runs prebuild)
/ios
/android
.kotlin/

# build and tool output
dist/
web-build/
.expo/
expo-env.d.ts
.metro-health-check*
*.tsbuildinfo

# local environment: never upload a developer's .env.local
.env*.local

# credentials and store config
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
*.pem

# Firebase config is supplied to the build as the GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON file
# variable, never as part of the project.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# noise
.DS_Store
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
*.orig.*
